### Option A: use the ready-made template (fastest)

1. Open the [Car Ownership and Preferences Survey template](/templates/car-ownership-and-preferences-survey-18446/) and click "Use Template."
2. Pick the questions from the five sections above that match the survey type you're running. Paste them in. Delete the defaults you don't need.
3. Turn on [conditional logic](/blog/what-is-conditional-logic-how-to-use-it/) where it helps. If a respondent picks "Full battery EV" in question 1 of the buying section, route them past gasoline-related questions and into the EV-specific block.
4. Hit Share. You get a public link, a [QR code](/features/qr-code-generator/), and an [embed snippet](/features/embed-forms/) for your dealership website, post-sale email, or service follow-up SMS.
5. Watch responses land. Filter by submission date, export to CSV, or pipe into Google Sheets via the [integration](/integrations/).

### Option B: generate a custom survey with AI

1. Open the [Formester AI Survey Generator](/ai-survey-generator/). Paste a topic ("post-service satisfaction for a luxury dealership"), upload a PDF (your existing question bank), or paste a URL.
2. The model writes a 10–25 question draft with answer scales. Review, edit, drop anything off-brand.
3. Share via link, QR, or embed. Same dashboard as Option A.

Both paths give you live response analytics, including CSAT and NPS calculations if you tag the score questions correctly. The [analytics view](/features/form-analytics/) handles the math; you don't.

