<p class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__intro">CSAT, NPS, CES, and the practical decisions behind a survey that gets sent and read.</p>
<div class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__list">

<details class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__item">
<summary>What is the difference between a car survey and a dealership survey?</summary>
<div class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__answer">A car survey scores the vehicle: reliability, build quality, fuel economy, range. A dealership survey scores the experience around the vehicle: sales floor, F&amp;I, delivery, service. Same customer, different teams own the result. Use Type 4 (reliability) above for the car, Type 2 (sales) and Type 3 (service) for the dealership.</div>
</details>

<details class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__item">
<summary>How many questions should a car survey have?</summary>
<div class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__answer">Eight to twelve for a post-sale or post-service email. Twenty to twenty-five for a market-research survey where you are paying for responses. Past 25 questions, drop-off climbs fast; response rates can fall ~50% past that threshold. Use <a href="https://formester.com/features/conditional-logic/">conditional logic</a> to keep the experience under 5 minutes even when the back-end bank is longer.</div>
</details>

<details class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__item">
<summary>What is a good NPS for a car dealership?</summary>
<div class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__answer">Industry-wide automotive NPS sits around +40 for mainstream franchise dealers and +60 for luxury and premium, per <a href="https://www.jdpower.com/business/press-releases/2024-us-customer-service-index-csi-study">J.D. Power&rsquo;s 2024 U.S. Customer Service Index Study</a>. Below +30, something specific is broken (often F&amp;I wait time or delivery walkthrough); above +70 you are outperforming the segment. Set up the calculation once in the Formester <a href="https://formester.com/blog/how-to-make-a-net-promoter-score-survey/">NPS guide</a>.</div>
</details>

<details class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__item">
<summary>When should I send a post-sale dealership survey?</summary>
<div class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__answer">Within 7 days of delivery, ideally within 72 hours. After day 10 the customer either forgot the specifics or already wrote a Google review you cannot change. For service surveys, the window is shorter: send within 48 hours of the bay handoff.</div>
</details>

<details class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__item">
<summary>How do I phrase rating-scale questions so the answers are usable?</summary>
<div class="fmstr-cmp-csq-faq__answer">Three rules: keep the scale consistent across the whole survey (1 to 5 stays 1 to 5; do not switch to 1 to 10 mid-form), label both endpoints clearly (1 = "Very dissatisfied", 5 = "Very satisfied", not just numbers), and reserve the 0 to 10 scale for the NPS question only. Phrase the question itself in plain English: "How transparent was the pricing, including all fees?" reads better than "Rate price transparency."</div>
</details>

